<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karo Batak</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Karo people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Karo <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batak">Batak</a> are a Batak people of the highlands of North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, around the Karo plateau above Medan. Linked to the coast by trade in forest products, they were connected with the Aru kingdom and later with the Deli Sultanate, which claimed authority over neighbouring Karo lands. Many converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in the twentieth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karo-batak.jpg" alt="Karo Batak" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Picsplease · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batak_Karo_Wedding.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
